# netbox — ws41: "user" loads with nginx's own warning when lobo is unprivileged,
# so the dry-run predicts. Before ws41 lobo -t refused this config on "user"
# alone (tests/config-corpus/INDEX.md, the blocked table).
args: --request 'GET http://localhost/'
exit: 0
--- expect
== request: GET http://localhost/
listener: [::]:18080
server: tests/config-corpus/netbox/conf.d/netbox.conf:34 [server_name _] — no server_name at this listener matches the request's host, so the listener's default answers (default_server, else the first server listening there)
  candidate server tests/config-corpus/netbox/conf.d/netbox.conf:1 [server_name netbox.example.com] — lost: not chosen for this listener and host (another server block answers it)
location: (none matched — the server block's own directives apply)
  precedence: = exact > longest prefix (regex is parse-only at this pin and never wins)
effective directives (the winning chain, with provenance):
  include       mime.types;  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:18
  default_type  application/octet-stream;  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:19
  log_format  main  '$remote_addr - $remote_user [$time_local] "$request" '
                      '$status $body_bytes_sent "$http_referer" '
                      '"$http_user_agent" "$http_x_forwarded_for"';  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:21
  access_log  logs/access.log  main;  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:25
  sendfile        on;  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:27
  keepalive_timeout  65;  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:30
  include conf.d/*.conf;  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:34
  listen [::]:18080 ipv6only=off;  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/conf.d/netbox.conf:36 (via tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:34)
  server_name _;  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/conf.d/netbox.conf:37 (via tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:34)
  return 301 https://$host$request_uri;  # from tests/config-corpus/netbox/conf.d/netbox.conf:38 (via tests/config-corpus/netbox/nginx.conf:34)
  note: parsed but not implemented at this pin, so they do not shape this decision: `default_type`, `sendfile`, `keepalive_timeout`, `return` (statuses: docs/directives.md)
decision: would answer 404 — no root/alias maps this path to the filesystem — the live server answers 404
